theory.intro:
The **magnitude** of a vector is its length, written $|\underset{\sim}{a}|$. Pythagoras' theorem on the components gives $|\underset{\sim}{a}|=\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}$. A length is never negative.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (4,3);
\coordinate (Q) at (4,0);
\draw[dashed] (O)--(Q) node[midway,below]{$x$};
\draw[dashed] (Q)--(P) node[midway,right]{$y$};
\draw[-{Stealth},thick] (O)--(P) node[midway,above left]{$|\underset{\sim}{a}|$};
\coordinate (r1) at ($(Q)!0.35cm!(O)$);
\coordinate (r2) at ($(Q)!0.35cm!(P)$);
\draw (r1)--($(r1)+(r2)-(Q)$)--(r2);
\node[above right] at (P) {$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
Find the magnitude of the vector $\underset{\sim}{a}$ shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.5]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (-1,-1) grid (9,9);
\draw[->] (-1.4,0)--(9.4,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.4)--(0,9.4) node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \i in {2,4,6,8} \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\i,0){$\i$};
\foreach \i in {2,4,6,8} \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,\i){$\i$};
\draw[-{Stealth},thick,blue] (0,0)--(6,8) node[above left]{$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.solution_text:
$\underset{\sim}{a}+\underset{\sim}{b}=\begin{pmatrix}4+(-1)\\1+5\end{pmatrix}$
$=\begin{pmatrix}3\\6\end{pmatrix}$
$|\underset{\sim}{a}+\underset{\sim}{b}|=\sqrt{3^{2}+6^{2}}$
$=\sqrt{9+36}$
$=\sqrt{45}$
$=3\sqrt{5}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.7]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[->] (-1.4,0)--(5.4,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.8)--(0,7.2) node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \i in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\i,0.12)--(\i,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\i,0){$\i$};}
\foreach \i in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\draw (0.12,\i)--(-0.12,\i); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,\i){$\i$};}
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0)--(4,1) node[midway,below right]{$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (4,1)--(3,6) node[midway,right]{$\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\draw[-{Stealth},thick,blue] (0,0)--(3,6) node[midway,above left]{$\underset{\sim}{a}+\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
